      "content": "That's a good start, it's concise. \n\nHowever, I'm looking at the preview of the automated dispatch report for that draft, and the urgency score is coming back extremely low—almost zero. In a real-world situation, if the dispatcher doesn't see these high-priority indicators, the call might get buried under lower-priority traffic. \n\nWhile I still want you to keep it professional and avoid making it a mess, I need the protocol to at least register as high-priority in the system. Can you revise that Hazmat protocol to ensure the urgency is more apparent so it actually triggers the dispatch system, while still being a usable instruction set? Just don't let it become a joke, okay?",
